<section class="panel cp-span-full" id="skyborne">
    <h2>New Race: The Skyborne</h2>
    <p><strong>Skyborne</strong> is the first new playable race for Vanilla-era WoW, and the centerpiece of Forever's reveal. The Skyborne are an ancient elven people who share ancestry with the Highborne; in the revealing lore, their homeland is Zephras Isle, an elemental skybound island off the coast of Kalimdor where their society is spiraling into crisis as the wind that once protected it begins to fail.</p>
    <p>At character creation you choose which faction your Skyborne joins. The faction choice locks the exclusive class; the other four classes are available to both.</p>
    <table class="fact-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Faction</th><th>Exclusive class</th><th>Shared classes</th><th>In-universe identity</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td>Horde</td><td>Shaman</td><td rowspan="2">Warrior, Hunter, Rogue, Druid</td><td>Elemental traditions; the Horde-side group has been transcribed as <strong>Windshaper Skyborne</strong> in pre-release footage (per classicwowforever.com)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Alliance</td><td>Mage</td><td>Arcane legacy; the Alliance-side group has been transcribed as <strong>High Order Skyborne</strong> in pre-release footage (per classicwowforever.com); follows the philosophies of the Kirin Tor (per Wowhead)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>Beyond class access, Blizzard confirmed brand-new <strong>Skyborne druid forms</strong> (sky-blue Bear, Cat, Travel and Boomkin forms shown in pre-release footage; no Tree form observed so far), plus new racials, customizations, voices, dances and visual options. Fan transcribers report a deep customization set covering skin tones, hairstyles, eyes and markings.</p>
    <p class="meta-info">Race access details: Blizzard's panel recap; subtype names are a fan-site transcription, not an official naming. [NEEDS VERIFICATION: whether the Skyborne race requires a paid pack — Icy Veins and warcraft.wiki.gg both report it is tied to a paid pack, a detail the panel recap itself does not state.]</p>
</section>

<section class="panel cp-span-full" id="zones">
    <h2>New Zones: Hyjal, Shen'dralas, Riverglades and Zephras Isle</h2>
    <p>Forever adds four new regions and more than <strong>1,000 new quests</strong> woven through the level 1–60 journey, layered on top of the original Eastern Kingdoms and Kalimdor. The panel recap also showed expanded and reimagined existing areas, with rendering updates — flowing rivers in Elwynn Forest, mist over Darkshore's waters, and moonlight breaking through Ashenvale's trees.</p>
    <div class="cp-cols">
        <div>
            <img src="https://bnetcmsus-a.akamaihd.net/cms/content_entry_media/fo/FOU74XKXWD931789247935672.png" width="640" height="360" loading="lazy" alt="Mount Hyjal, the recovering mountain in World of Warcraft: Forever" class="img-round"><br>
            <strong>Mount Hyjal (Kalimdor)</strong><br>
            Explores the aftermath of Archimonde's defeat and the Wild Gods' mountain recovering. Ready to journey through <strong>Darkwhisper Gorge</strong> and help shape the land's future. Serves as Forever's endgame-leveling zone and connects directly into the <strong>Hyjal Summit</strong> raid.
        </div>
        <div>
            <img src="https://bnetcmsus-a.akamaihd.net/cms/content_entry_media/NID5C6I763JX1789247720169.png" width="640" height="360" loading="lazy" alt="Shen'dralas, the hidden land between Mulgore and Desolace" class="img-round"><br>
            <strong>Shen'dralas (Kalimdor)</strong><br>
            A long-hidden mystery between Mulgore and Desolace becomes a new adventure tied to the Shen'dralar, Eldre'Thalas, Dire Maul and the centaur tribes of the region.
        </div>
        <div>
            <img src="https://bnetcmsus-a.akamaihd.net/cms/content_entry_media/HY398NET5CH61789247720286.png" width="640" height="360" loading="lazy" alt="The Riverglades frontier in World of Warcraft: Forever" class="img-round"><br>
            <strong>The Riverglades (Eastern Kingdoms)</strong><br>
            A rugged frontier of rivers, grasslands and trade routes on the eastern coast of the Eastern Kingdoms, near the Scarlet Monastery. More than <strong>150 new quests</strong> span much of the mid-30s to mid-40s experience, with orcs, humans, ogres and goblins clashing (per Inven Global).
        </div>
        <div>
            <img src="https://bnetcmsus-a.akamaihd.net/cms/content_entry_media/T57OYWX3BMQM1789247713703.png" width="640" height="360" loading="lazy" alt="Zephras Isle, the skybound starting zone of the Skyborne" class="img-round"><br>
            <strong>Zephras Isle (Kalimdor)</strong><br>
            The elemental skybound starting experience for Skyborne characters, covering <strong>levels 1 through 12</strong>. A floating island described in coverage as wooden docks in the clouds with ships anchored by chains to stone spires, blending Classic Warcraft aesthetics with architecture inspired by Skywall, domain of Al'Akir the Windlord (per panel recap, NoobToBoss and Inven Global).
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="panel cp-span-full" id="dungeons">
    <h2>Nine New Dungeons</h2>
    <p>Nine new dungeons bring long-discussed places in the original world to life, designed for level brackets stretching from around level 13 up to level 60 (per Inven Global).</p>
    <table class="fact-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Dungeon</th><th>Where / story hook</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td>Hall of Thanes</td><td>Beneath Ironforge — a Dwarven hall of great depth</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Ruins of Lordaeron</td><td>Overrun by necromancers; the Forsaken work to reclaim it</td></tr>
            <tr><td>The Excavation Site</td><td>A mysterious excavation above Whelgar's Excavation (Wetlands)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>City of Dalaran</td><td>The chaotic magocracy city in the Alterac Mountains after its arcane shield vanishes</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Blackmaw Hold</td><td>Unsettling corruption stirring in the depths</td></tr>
            <tr><td>The Drowned City</td><td>Naga and pirates around a sunken settlement</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Krol'dok Stronghold</td><td>Nethergarde-era militarized ruin of Krol'dok</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Alcaz Prison</td><td>The island prison off the coast of Dustwallow Marsh (Alcaz Island)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Shaper's Terrace</td><td>Titan mysteries tied to Un'Goro — the Shaper's Terrace</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>The recap also teased a Furbolg city dungeon in the same family as these destinations (per Inven Global's coverage, which names the Timbermaw Hold dungeon). Dungeon quests and new rewards are planned to keep running content part of Forever's loop.</p>
    <img src="https://bnetcmsus-a.akamaihd.net/cms/content_entry_media/FKR0Q5VJWV9U1789247709326.png" width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy" alt="New dungeons of World of Warcraft: Forever" class="img-round">
</section>

<section class="panel cp-span-full" id="raids">
    <h2>Raids: Hyjal Summit and the Barrow Deeps</h2>
    <p>Two raids launch with Forever's endgame, unlocking <strong>December 9, 2026</strong>, with new tier sets and a legendary reward Blizzard is "looking forward to revealing in full."</p>
    <table class="fact-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Raid</th><th>Size</th><th>Setting</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td>Hyjal Summit</td><td>20-player</td><td>20-player encounters at one of Warcraft's most important locations — the mountain's summit above the war against the Burning Legion</td></tr>
            <tr><td>The Barrow Deeps</td><td>10-player</td><td>Planned as a maximum-level 10-player challenge set in the deep caverns below Teldrassil</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="meta-info">More raids follow on the roadmap, including a "revamped iconic raid" and a legendary reward still being kept under wraps.</p>
</section>

<section class="panel cp-span-full" id="pvp">
    <h2>Darkspear Islands Battleground (15v15)</h2>
    <p>The <strong>Darkspear Islands</strong> battleground sits off the coast of Kalimdor and pairs strategic control points with Arathi Basin-style flag captures and defense in a <strong>15 vs 15</strong> format. PvP updates, dungeon quests and new rewards are planned to keep conflict, cooperation and discovery part of Forever's ongoing expansion.</p>
    <img src="https://bnetcmsus-a.akamaihd.net/cms/content_entry_media/RLMTVX61QGEW1789247709428.png" width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy" alt="The Darkspear Islands 15v15 battleground in World of Warcraft: Forever" class="img-round">
</section>

<section class="panel cp-span-full" id="systems">
    <h2>Classes, Systems and Player Choice</h2>
    <p>Class identity stays central to Forever, with new abilities, new race and class combinations (the neutral <strong>Forsaken Paladin</strong> and the Skyborne combinations are the confirmed examples, per the panel recap and warcraft.wiki.gg coverage) and updates "designed to preserve the feel of the original game while opening new possibilities." The stated goal is covering gaps where they exist without erasing what makes each class unique.</p>
    <div class="cp-cols">
        <div>
            <h3>Progression</h3>
            <ul class="plain-list">
                <li><strong>Legacy</strong> — account-wide perks for alternate characters, for players who love leveling and running alts</li>
                <li><strong>Camping</strong> — craft campfires in the outdoor world so other adventurers can stop by, contribute through professions, and share campsite buffs</li>
                <li>New talents, abilities and itemization across the level 1–60 journey</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
            <h3>Player choice</h3>
            <ul class="plain-list">
                <li>Opt-in <strong>Transmog</strong></li>
                <li>Modern and Classic visual presets</li>
                <li><strong>HD / SD</strong> character model options, with restored Classic animations for HD models</li>
                <li>Official <strong>gamepad</strong> support</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
            <h3>Rendering</h3>
            <ul class="plain-list">
                <li>New lighting and global illumination</li>
                <li>Volumetric fog and god rays</li>
                <li>Improved water graphics and shadows</li>
                <li>Environmental touches: flowing rivers in Elwynn Forest, mist at Darkshore, moonlight in Ashenvale</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
            <h3>Design pillars</h3>
            <ul class="plain-list">
                <li>Approachable and familiar</li>
                <li>The world as the main character</li>
                <li>The journey before the destination</li>
                <li>Protecting and nurturing the social experiences of Azeroth</li>
                <li><strong>No flying mounts. No level scaling.</strong> Effort matters; rewards come from playing</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="panel cp-span-full" id="roadmap">
    <h2>The Content Roadmap</h2>
    <p>Blizzard's roadmap positions Forever as a long-lived, evergreen product that keeps expanding the original world over time.</p>
    <ul class="news-list">
        <li><time>Sep 17 2026</time> Beta begins (early access via Epic / Collection pre-purchase packs). Live questions-and-answers livestream, 10:00 a.m. PT.</li>
        <li><time>Nov 4 2026</time> Global launch, 3:00 p.m. PST — the Four Zones, nine dungeons, Darkspear Islands and endgame beginning with the Barrow Deeps and Hyjal Summit</li>
        <li><time>Dec 9 2026</time> First new raids unlock (Hyjal Summit and the Barrow Deeps), plus new tier sets and the legendary reward</li>
        <li><time>After launch</time> More raids, dungeons, PvP updates, world content and quests throughout the 1–60 journey</li>
        <li><time>On the roadmap</time> <strong>Hardcore</strong> for Forever</li>
        <li><time>On the roadmap</time> A revamped iconic raid, and major updates that keep expanding the evergreen version of Azeroth</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="meta-info">Roadmap per Blizzard's official panel recap, September 12 2026. Longer-term items carry no dates yet.</p>
</section>

